are suffering from asthma?

01:13:04.130 --> 01:13:07.600
- Yeah, it is a great question.

01:13:07.600 --> 01:13:09.843
And let me just see if I can just pull up,

01:13:11.750 --> 01:13:13.870
so it's a great question.

01:13:13.870 --> 01:13:16.830
So what I can say about
it right off the cuff

01:13:16.830 --> 01:13:19.410
is that people that are incarcerated

01:13:19.410 --> 01:13:22.090
have higher rates of asthma

01:13:22.090 --> 01:13:24.570
compared to the general population.

01:13:24.570 --> 01:13:27.400
In fact, they have higher
rates of hypertension,

01:13:27.400 --> 01:13:31.556
they have higher rates of heart disease,

01:13:31.556 --> 01:13:33.660
and then certainly have hepatitis C.

01:13:33.660 --> 01:13:35.360
So people that have been incarcerated

01:13:35.360 --> 01:13:37.830
have kind of disproportionately
higher rates.

01:13:37.830 --> 01:13:40.266
And then look at got this,

01:13:40.266 --> 01:13:42.683
I'm gonna just share the screen, so yeah.

01:13:46.510 --> 01:13:47.343
Here we go.

01:13:50.100 --> 01:13:53.216
- Yeah, she-
- You don't see that?

01:13:53.216 --> 01:13:55.360
- No, I don't see, it's coming up.

01:13:55.360 --> 01:13:57.520
There we go.
- Okay, there we go.

01:13:57.520 --> 01:13:59.310
And these are data that are taken

01:13:59.310 --> 01:14:02.593
again from a Bureau of
Justice Statistics survey.

01:14:05.163 --> 01:14:06.080
You know, I just realized

01:14:06.080 --> 01:14:07.460
I had never kind of defined this though

01:14:07.460 --> 01:14:09.170
this might be just real
basic for you guys,

01:14:09.170 --> 01:14:10.810
but jails and prisons are different,

01:14:10.810 --> 01:14:13.020
so jails house those people

01:14:13.020 --> 01:14:14.770
that are waiting judicational crimes

01:14:14.770 --> 01:14:18.510
or serving sentences of less than a year

01:14:18.510 --> 01:14:20.810
and then prisons house those
that have been sentenced

01:14:20.810 --> 01:14:25.010
typically for sentences
longer than a year.

01:14:25.010 --> 01:14:28.420
And so these data come from the
Bureau of Justice Statistics

01:14:28.420 --> 01:14:31.960
and so what you can see
here last row here asthma is

01:14:32.950 --> 01:14:36.600
that it's 14.9% in the prison population

01:14:36.600 --> 01:14:38.810
compared to the general population at 10.2

01:14:38.810 --> 01:14:42.350
and the jail population
is 20.1 compared to 11.4.

01:14:42.350 --> 01:14:46.880
And these are data from 2011 to 2012,

01:14:47.820 --> 01:14:50.850
but are probably, they'd be the same here.

01:14:50.850 --> 01:14:52.543
It's disproportionately higher.

01:14:53.680 --> 01:14:57.130
And as is the case for
many chronic conditions

01:14:57.130 --> 01:15:01.492
cervical cancer, it goes on and on.

01:15:01.492 --> 01:15:04.360
- And we are running close to time,

01:15:04.360 --> 01:15:06.820
so I'm gonna ask the final question.

01:15:06.820 --> 01:15:11.820
And the question is what can,
